AgentInterview — Codex Handoff

Create a new repository named AgentInterview.

Objective

Build a self-contained, deterministic evaluation framework for comparing AI models, prompts, agent configurations, and multi-agent workflows.

Each evaluation must resemble a standardized engineering interview. Every run must receive the same immutable project, instructions, fixtures, and graders.

Do not evaluate against an existing or living application.

Core Requirements

Each interview must be an isolated package containing:

* a versioned manifest
* candidate-visible instructions
* a complete starter project
* local dependencies
* visible tests when appropriate
* hidden deterministic graders
* expected artifacts
* resource limits
* scoring rules

A run must follow this lifecycle:

1. Load an interview package.
2. Create a clean temporary workspace.
3. Copy the starter project.
4. Execute the selected agent configuration.
5. Capture model and agent traces.
6. Run deterministic graders.
7. Calculate scores.
8. persist a machine-readable result.
9. Generate a human-readable report.

Determinism Rules

* No dependency on company source code.
* No dependency on mutable external services.
* No internet access during an interview.
* Pin all package and runtime versions.
* Freeze clocks and random seeds when relevant.
* Run each attempt in a clean environment.
* Do not use an LLM as the authoritative grader.
* Correctness must be determined by tests, schemas, snapshots, static analysis, performance thresholds, or exact comparisons.
* Interview definitions must be immutable once published. Changes require a new version.

